# Python conventions

The full **Code style** section lives in `AGENTS.md` — read it. In short:

- Type-annotate every function signature. Prefer explicit over clever; don't
  add dependencies or abstractions without a concrete need.
- Read configuration from `src/config/settings.py` (`get_settings()`) — no
  hard-coded URLs, keys, or paths.
- Route all model access through `src/core/llm/provider.py`, and keep the
  `noop` provider working so the tool runs without an API key.
- New CLI commands go in `src/cli/commands/` (one file per command) and are
  registered in `src/cli/main.py`; new API routes in `src/api/routes/`.
